    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap split">
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Not every surface can handle a blast of high pressure. Render, painted cladding, weatherboards and roof tiles can be damaged by aggressive cleaning — which is exactly why soft washing exists. Using low pressure and specialised, biodegradable cleaning solutions, soft washing gently breaks down mould, mildew, algae and grime at the source, then rinses it away for a clean, even finish that lasts.</p><p>Stan The Man Cleaning offers professional soft washing across Melbourne's Eastern Suburbs. It's the safest way to refresh your home's façade and roofline, restoring that clean, cared-for look without putting your surfaces at risk.</p>
          <h2>What's included</h2>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>Low-pressure washing of house exteriors and façades</li>
            <li>Render, cladding, weatherboard and painted surfaces</li>
            <li>Roof soft washing to remove moss, lichen and algae</li>
            <li>Eaves, fascias and gutters exterior cleaned</li>
            <li>Biodegradable, surface-safe cleaning solutions</li>
            <li>Even, streak-free finish that lasts longer than a rinse</li>
          </ul>
          <h2>Why soft washing beats high pressure on delicate surfaces</h2>
          <p>High pressure can crack render, strip paint, force water under cladding and dislodge roof tiles. Soft washing avoids all of that. Because it treats the organic growth chemically rather than just blasting the surface, it also keeps mould and algae away for longer — so your home stays cleaner between visits. It's the smart, gentle choice for rendered homes, painted exteriors and roofs across the Eastern Suburbs.</p>
          <h3>Servicing your local area</h3>
          <p>We regularly work in Donvale, Doncaster, Doncaster East, Templestowe, Warrandyte, Park Orchards, Ringwood, Mitcham, Nunawading, Blackburn, Box Hill, Balwyn, Bulleen and Eltham. If you're anywhere in Melbourne's Eastern Suburbs, we'd love to help.</p>
